From b61950fac59684490fa2290662a7218408ba9888 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 02:54:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] tests/k8s: first multi-tenant E2E scenario
 (TestMultiTenantSanity)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extends the existing kind+Helm harness with the smallest E2E that
proves multi-tenant routing is end-to-end correct on a real patched
binary in a real cluster: two tenants share one mock LLM, each gets
its own tenant-scoped provider+VK via /api/platform/tenants +
/api/tenants/{tid}/{providers,governance/virtual-keys}, both drive a
chat completion through their own runtime, then tenant A's VK gets
deleted and we assert (a) A can no longer drive inference and (b) B
still can — closing the loop on patch 0028's same-replica resolver
cache invalidation.

Harness extensions:

- fixtures/bifrost.go gains a functional-options API:
  - WithMultiTenant(adminDefaultTenant) splices
    BIFROST_MULTI_TENANT_ENABLED=true (+ optional
    BIFROST_ADMIN_DEFAULT_TENANT) into the rendered Deployment
    BEFORE kubectl apply, so the very first pod that comes up
    already carries the right config. Doing this pre-apply (rather
    than `kubectl set env` after) avoids the race where WaitReady
    picks up an old-spec pod that briefly became Ready.
  - WithExtraEnv(name, value) is a generic escape hatch for
    future scenarios that need other env knobs.
  - Splicing uses yaml.v3 (already an indirect dep, now promoted
    to direct) on the rendered YAML rather than sed/regex so
    reformatting / comments don't trip a brittle string match.

- fixtures/multitenant.go (new) — MTAdmin raw-HTTP client driving
  the per-tenant admin surface the F5XC patches add. The
  go-bifrost-ai SDK doesn't yet know about /api/tenants/{tid}/...,
  so scenarios drive these endpoints over plain http.Client.
  Surface: CreateTenant, CreateProvider, CreateProviderKey,
  CreateVirtualKey, ListVirtualKeys, DeleteVirtualKey, Chat,
  WaitForVKResolver (bounded retry to absorb cold-start lazy
  load).

- scenarios/multitenant_sanity_test.go (new) — TestMultiTenantSanity:
  the integration test described above. //go:build k8s, runs under
  the existing `make test-k8s-image` + GOWORK=off path.

- README.md updated with the new test entry and a short
  "Multi-tenant scenarios" section pointing at the harness
  extensions, so follow-on scenarios (streaming, async, MCP,
  multi-replica, Anthropic-shape) can layer onto the same MTAdmin.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
